  "id": "thin-slices-of-behavior",
  "term": "thin slices of behavior",
  "definition": "Thin slices of behavior are brief samples of a person’s observable actions or manner that observers use to make quick judgments about that person, such as whether they are likely to cooperate or defect. In this source, the term refers to short stretches of behavior examined for clues that might reveal social tendencies.",
